# =====================================================
# PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# =====================================================
# For Vercel deployment, add these to your environment variables
# NEVER commit these values to your repository!

# Supabase Configuration
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key_for_frontend
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_for_backend

# Next.js Configuration
NEXTAUTH_URL=https://your-vercel-app-url.vercel.app
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your_nextauth_secret_key

# =====================================================
# SECURITY IMPLEMENTATION FOR PRODUCTION
# =====================================================

# 1. CLIENT-SIDE (Frontend): Use ANON key
#    - Only for read operations
#    - With RLS policies enforced
#    - User authentication handled by your app

# 2. SERVER-SIDE (API Routes): Use SERVICE_ROLE key  
#    - For write operations
#    - Bypasses RLS (but you control access in code)
#    - Validate user sessions before database operations

# 3. AUTHENTICATION FLOW:
#    - Users login through your custom auth
#    - Store session in httpOnly cookies (not localStorage)
#    - Validate sessions on server-side before database access
#    - Use middleware to protect API routes

# =====================================================
# DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST
# =====================================================

# ✅ Database Security:
# - RLS enabled on all tables
# - Service role key kept secret
# - Policies allow controlled access

# ✅ Application Security:
# - Move authentication to server-side
# - Use httpOnly cookies for sessions
# - Validate all database operations
# - Rate limiting on API endpoints

# ✅ Environment Security:
# - All secrets in Vercel env vars
# - No hardcoded credentials
# - Separate keys for dev/prod

# ✅ Network Security:
# - HTTPS enforced
# - CORS properly configured
# - API routes protected by middleware
